vent": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LprSPWVxDim1EQVHua7k1X", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_timeout"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 420230, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LprSPWVxDim1EQVHua7k1X", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 424121, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch and CI passed. I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). So the 2.665 case rounded to 2.67, but the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR: that needs a code owner to approve it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WYL6gn2uw6Uqnwp2jJPk1d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NqGLB2pYXCBUnrDcr1hKXz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012ZuoFqxFv8rL2fYjqkXa7g", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LEWKbVSpwbTstyE4K2N4E6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NTRPvQDpHs6JtUwCNb5pvm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LMixkBvEdhrabZJHa8VhGH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-round-half-even", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015kV2a7poxgqVWufvdUEbwg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LprSPWVxDim1EQVHua7k1X", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. Because of this, `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed and broke the nightly build.\n\nThis PR switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch and CI passed. I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). So the 2.665 case rounded to 2.67, but the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR: that needs a code owner to approve it.", "type": "text"}]}]}